  {
    "name": "a5a6d04764b310e2941b",
    "visualType": "columnChart",
    "title": "Denials by reason",
    "demonstrates": "seven reasons, 1,079 to 1,175 each. A near-uniform mix is a WORKLOAD profile, not a root cause - there is no dominant failure to go and fix. Columns rather than bars because seven categories scroll in a 228 px bar chart and the seventh would be hidden"
  },
  {
    "name": "9b6f397d929321ad9c3f",
    "visualType": "treemap",
    "title": "Denied value by category and reason",
    "demonstrates": "treemap: grouped the way a denials team is organised - front-end, coding, clinical, process - so the categories name who would own the fix"
  },
  {
    "name": "5f1dae207401b3e8ae9a",
    "visualType": "columnChart",
    "title": "Denial rate by payer",
    "demonstrates": "the one real split in the data, and the bar colour says which: Self Pay in the accent, the five insurers in one muted tone because they do not differ from each other"
  },
  {
    "name": "3954c269638ab2887c19",
    "visualType": "pieChart",
    "title": "The denials queue, by workflow state",
    "demonstrates": "pie: Open, Appealed, Corrected, Written Off. These are WORKFLOW STATES, not outcomes - see the note"
  },
  {
    "name": "55427fc06156ed75f5bd",
    "visualType": "lineChart",
    "title": "Denial rate by adjudication month",
    "demonstrates": "flat at 7-8% for 44 months. There is no deterioration and no improvement to explain"
  },
